\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Model architecture. A:~Agent grid ($N_r \times N_c$) with three states (Buy, Hold, Sell). Green boundary cells are edge agents; dashed-border interior cells follow the minority rule~(19286); solid interior cells follow the majority rule~(19280). The highlighted cell and its Von~Neumann neighbors are expanded in~B. B:~CA update: the four neighbor states are summed to produce~$c_{r,c}$, which indexes into the rule table to determine the next state~$s'_{r,c}$. In this example $c_{r,c}=5$, so both rules output Sell; the two rules differ only at $c \in \{0,1\}$. C:~Model~A (open): exogenous QQQ prices (black trace) fluctuate within a Bollinger Band (gray region). Band breakouts set the edge-agent state, which is injected into the grid boundary. D:~Model~B (feedback-closed): the grid's net order imbalance~$\varphi _\tau $ feeds back (orange arrow) to update an endogenous price, closing a reflexive loop.}}{3}{figure.caption.3}\protected@file@percent }
\providecommand*\caption@xref[2]{\@setref\relax\@undefined{#1}}
\newlabel{fig:schematic}{{1}{3}{Model architecture. A:~Agent grid ($N_r \times N_c$) with three states (Buy, Hold, Sell). Green boundary cells are edge agents; dashed-border interior cells follow the minority rule~(19286); solid interior cells follow the majority rule~(19280). The highlighted cell and its Von~Neumann neighbors are expanded in~B. B:~CA update: the four neighbor states are summed to produce~$c_{r,c}$, which indexes into the rule table to determine the next state~$s'_{r,c}$. In this example $c_{r,c}=5$, so both rules output Sell; the two rules differ only at $c \in \{0,1\}$. C:~Model~A (open): exogenous QQQ prices (black trace) fluctuate within a Bollinger Band (gray region). Band breakouts set the edge-agent state, which is injected into the grid boundary. D:~Model~B (feedback-closed): the grid's net order imbalance~$\varphi _\tau $ feeds back (orange arrow) to update an endogenous price, closing a reflexive loop}{figure.caption.3}{}}
