\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces Theory overview for Model~A (Rules~19280/19286). A:~Potts energy~$e$ and site entropy~$S_1$ vs.\ minority fraction~$f$ ($128 \times 128$ lattice, periodic boundaries, time-averaged over $2{,}000$ steps). The mixed attractor persists at $e \approx -0.37$ and $S_1 \approx 1.06$; above the transition the system collapses to the all-Sell state at $e \approx -0.93$ and $S_1 \approx 0.18$, a sharp finite-size drop ($\Delta e \approx 0.56$, $\Delta S_1 \approx 0.88$); near the crossover the $2{,}000$-step averages retain the mixed state because metastable lifetimes exceed the window, so the crossover completes to the right of the marked $f_c$. B:~Spectral radius of the pair-approximation Jacobian at the uncorrelated fixed point, declining monotonically from $0.95$ at $f = 0$ to $0.71$ at $f = 0.5$, strictly below the instability threshold (dashed line at~$1$). This tested pair closure does not capture the crossover. C:~Sell-cluster sizes in the mixed state (log scale): largest cluster ever observed (orange) and mean largest per snapshot (black), over 100 snapshots of a $128 \times 128$ lattice. The mean largest cluster (black) holds at ${\sim }30$--$60$~cells in the subcritical mixed state, while the largest observed cluster (orange) reaches ${\sim }400$~cells near $f = 0.145$ and exceeds $1{,}800$~cells by $f = 0.16$ (the dip at $f = 0.155$ is a single-realization fluctuation of the fixed-seed protocol). Dashed vertical lines mark the midpoint $f=0.145$ of the observed $[0.14,0.15]$ bracket.}}{12}{figure.caption.34}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:theory-overview}{{4}{12}{Theory overview for Model~A (Rules~19280/19286). A:~Potts energy~$e$ and site entropy~$S_1$ vs.\ minority fraction~$f$ ($128 \times 128$ lattice, periodic boundaries, time-averaged over $2{,}000$ steps). The mixed attractor persists at $e \approx -0.37$ and $S_1 \approx 1.06$; above the transition the system collapses to the all-Sell state at $e \approx -0.93$ and $S_1 \approx 0.18$, a sharp finite-size drop ($\Delta e \approx 0.56$, $\Delta S_1 \approx 0.88$); near the crossover the $2{,}000$-step averages retain the mixed state because metastable lifetimes exceed the window, so the crossover completes to the right of the marked $f_c$. B:~Spectral radius of the pair-approximation Jacobian at the uncorrelated fixed point, declining monotonically from $0.95$ at $f = 0$ to $0.71$ at $f = 0.5$, strictly below the instability threshold (dashed line at~$1$). This tested pair closure does not capture the crossover. C:~Sell-cluster sizes in the mixed state (log scale): largest cluster ever observed (orange) and mean largest per snapshot (black), over 100 snapshots of a $128 \times 128$ lattice. The mean largest cluster (black) holds at ${\sim }30$--$60$~cells in the subcritical mixed state, while the largest observed cluster (orange) reaches ${\sim }400$~cells near $f = 0.145$ and exceeds $1{,}800$~cells by $f = 0.16$ (the dip at $f = 0.155$ is a single-realization fluctuation of the fixed-seed protocol). Dashed vertical lines mark the midpoint $f=0.145$ of the observed $[0.14,0.15]$ bracket}{figure.caption.34}{}}
