\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {7}{\ignorespaces Birth locations of the onset cluster. (Top left) Map of the founding cell of the largest sell cluster at crash onset across the $39$ boundary-versus-bulk runs that nucleated, labeled on the interior alone so that a bulk birth can be told apart from attachment to the active-edge ring. (Top right and bottom left) Histograms of the founding cell's distance from the nearest boundary, for the $20$ freeze and $19$ collapse runs separately, each against the uniform-null expectation. Births were bulk-dominated and consistent with a uniform distribution: the pooled fraction founded within distance~$2$ of the boundary was $0.077$, below rather than above the $0.125$ uniform null and statistically indistinguishable from it (binomial $p = 0.47$), with a median founding distance of $12$ cells into the deep bulk. (Bottom right) Timing of ring attachment relative to birth and onset for the runs whose growing cluster reached the active-edge ring before onset---$6$ of $19$ collapse runs and $0$ of $20$ freeze runs---the edge asserting itself only after birth. The winning nucleus is born in the bulk, not templated by the boundary.}}{17}{figure.caption.53}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:mb-birthsites}{{7}{17}{Birth locations of the onset cluster. (Top left) Map of the founding cell of the largest sell cluster at crash onset across the $39$ boundary-versus-bulk runs that nucleated, labeled on the interior alone so that a bulk birth can be told apart from attachment to the active-edge ring. (Top right and bottom left) Histograms of the founding cell's distance from the nearest boundary, for the $20$ freeze and $19$ collapse runs separately, each against the uniform-null expectation. Births were bulk-dominated and consistent with a uniform distribution: the pooled fraction founded within distance~$2$ of the boundary was $0.077$, below rather than above the $0.125$ uniform null and statistically indistinguishable from it (binomial $p = 0.47$), with a median founding distance of $12$ cells into the deep bulk. (Bottom right) Timing of ring attachment relative to birth and onset for the runs whose growing cluster reached the active-edge ring before onset---$6$ of $19$ collapse runs and $0$ of $20$ freeze runs---the edge asserting itself only after birth. The winning nucleus is born in the bulk, not templated by the boundary}{figure.caption.53}{}}
