\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {9}{\ignorespaces Stamped-patch seeding outcomes across placements and configurations. (Top row) Onset step per seed under each arm---an unstamped control and a $3 \times 3$ sell patch stamped at edge, mid, and center placements---for the freeze (left) and collapse (right) configurations, with gray lines pairing the same seed across arms; the pairings cross in both directions and no placement advances onset. The apparent delay under the freeze mid placement (median paired onset advance $-257$ steps, sign-flip $p = 0.0238$) is exploratory---uncorrected across the six-test family and failing the Bonferroni threshold of $0.0083$---a lead, not a result. (Middle row) Dominance rate per placement: the fraction of runs in which the cluster standing largest at onset descends from the stamped patch is $0/20$ in every one of the six configuration-by-placement cells. (Bottom row) Largest-cluster growth trajectories for a single exemplar seed under each arm: which arm reaches domain scale first differs between the two configurations rather than tracking the stamped placement, and the domain that grows is in every run one founded away from the patch.}}{21}{figure.caption.58}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:mb-seeding}{{9}{21}{Stamped-patch seeding outcomes across placements and configurations. (Top row) Onset step per seed under each arm---an unstamped control and a $3 \times 3$ sell patch stamped at edge, mid, and center placements---for the freeze (left) and collapse (right) configurations, with gray lines pairing the same seed across arms; the pairings cross in both directions and no placement advances onset. The apparent delay under the freeze mid placement (median paired onset advance $-257$ steps, sign-flip $p = 0.0238$) is exploratory---uncorrected across the six-test family and failing the Bonferroni threshold of $0.0083$---a lead, not a result. (Middle row) Dominance rate per placement: the fraction of runs in which the cluster standing largest at onset descends from the stamped patch is $0/20$ in every one of the six configuration-by-placement cells. (Bottom row) Largest-cluster growth trajectories for a single exemplar seed under each arm: which arm reaches domain scale first differs between the two configurations rather than tracking the stamped placement, and the domain that grows is in every run one founded away from the patch}{figure.caption.58}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {10}{\ignorespaces Front velocity against absolute budget suppression at $f = 0.20$. (Left) For the $97$ runs included across the five cash doses ($250$--$5{,}000$; $3$ runs excluded by the window rule), the front velocity---the OLS slope of the front extent over the onset-aligned window $[t_{\mathrm  {on}}+50,\,t_{\mathrm  {on}}+400]$---is plotted against the mean absolute number of suppressed buy orders per step over the same window, colored by dose with the per-cash medians marked as diamonds; velocity falls as suppression rises, Spearman $\rho = -0.372$, permutation $p = 0.0003$. (Right) The same velocities arranged by initial cash on a logarithmic axis, with a bar at each per-dose median: the medians are U-shaped in cash---highest at cash $250$, lowest near $1{,}000$--$2{,}000$, rising again at $5{,}000$---while the per-dose median suppression spans only $517$--$595$ orders per step, so the supported claim is the pooled and within-dose velocity--suppression relationship, not a monotone ordering by dose.}}{22}{figure.caption.59}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:mb-velsupp}{{10}{22}{Front velocity against absolute budget suppression at $f = 0.20$. (Left) For the $97$ runs included across the five cash doses ($250$--$5{,}000$; $3$ runs excluded by the window rule), the front velocity---the OLS slope of the front extent over the onset-aligned window $[t_{\mathrm {on}}+50,\,t_{\mathrm {on}}+400]$---is plotted against the mean absolute number of suppressed buy orders per step over the same window, colored by dose with the per-cash medians marked as diamonds; velocity falls as suppression rises, Spearman $\rho = -0.372$, permutation $p = 0.0003$. (Right) The same velocities arranged by initial cash on a logarithmic axis, with a bar at each per-dose median: the medians are U-shaped in cash---highest at cash $250$, lowest near $1{,}000$--$2{,}000$, rising again at $5{,}000$---while the per-dose median suppression spans only $517$--$595$ orders per step, so the supported claim is the pooled and within-dose velocity--suppression relationship, not a monotone ordering by dose}{figure.caption.59}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {11}{\ignorespaces Budget-toggle intervention: paired, onset-aligned counterfactuals at $f = 0.20$ with a $W = 400$ post-toggle window (Section~\ref {sec:mb-protocols}). (Left column) Largest sell cluster as a fraction of the grid against steps since onset, for the three arms---injection (cash $\times 10$ at onset, on the tight cash-$500$ base) and the mild ($\times 0.1$) and harsh ($\times 0.01$) withdrawals, both on the loose cash-$5{,}000$ base---with each toggled trajectory (color) drawn over its control (gray) for the $19$ included seed pairs per arm; the dashed line marks the toggle at $t_{\mathrm  {on}}$, and the pre-toggle trajectories coincide by construction. (Right column) Paired front velocities over the window, one line per seed pair, control against toggled: injection accelerates the front in $14$ of $19$ pairs (sign test $p = 0.064$), while withdrawal is null at both doses (sign-flip permutation $p = 0.67$ mild, $p = 0.29$ harsh).}}{23}{figure.caption.61}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:mb-toggle}{{11}{23}{Budget-toggle intervention: paired, onset-aligned counterfactuals at $f = 0.20$ with a $W = 400$ post-toggle window (Section~\ref {sec:mb-protocols}). (Left column) Largest sell cluster as a fraction of the grid against steps since onset, for the three arms---injection (cash $\times 10$ at onset, on the tight cash-$500$ base) and the mild ($\times 0.1$) and harsh ($\times 0.01$) withdrawals, both on the loose cash-$5{,}000$ base---with each toggled trajectory (color) drawn over its control (gray) for the $19$ included seed pairs per arm; the dashed line marks the toggle at $t_{\mathrm {on}}$, and the pre-toggle trajectories coincide by construction. (Right column) Paired front velocities over the window, one line per seed pair, control against toggled: injection accelerates the front in $14$ of $19$ pairs (sign test $p = 0.064$), while withdrawal is null at both doses (sign-flip permutation $p = 0.67$ mild, $p = 0.29$ harsh)}{figure.caption.61}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {12}{\ignorespaces Edge-ring trace of the price-to-boundary conduit around the toggle. Each panel draws an edge-ring state fraction, averaged over the $19$ included seed pairs and aligned at the per-seed onset, for the toggled arm (color) against its control (gray), with the dashed line marking the toggle at $t_{\mathrm  {on}}$: the ring's Buy fraction occupies the left column and its Sell fraction the right, one row per arm (injection $\times 10$; mild withdrawal $\times 0.1$; harsh withdrawal $\times 0.01$), and the pre-toggle traces coincide by construction. (Top row) Injection flips the ring at the toggle---from ${\sim }0.5$ Buy and $0$ Sell in the control to $0$ Buy and ${\sim }1.0$ Sell---and the flipped state decays back over the following $100$--$200$ steps as the EMA bands catch up with the supported price. (Middle and bottom rows) Withdrawal transiently deepens an already-engaged brake: the control ring sits near $0.46$ Buy after onset, either cut lifts the Buy fraction to ${\sim }0.72$--$0.74$ before the transient excess dissipates by ${\sim }200$ steps, and the Sell fraction---which in this loose configuration declines from ${\sim }0.37$ well before onset to zero just after---remains indistinguishable between control and toggled throughout.}}{24}{figure.caption.62}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:mb-edgetrace}{{12}{24}{Edge-ring trace of the price-to-boundary conduit around the toggle. Each panel draws an edge-ring state fraction, averaged over the $19$ included seed pairs and aligned at the per-seed onset, for the toggled arm (color) against its control (gray), with the dashed line marking the toggle at $t_{\mathrm {on}}$: the ring's Buy fraction occupies the left column and its Sell fraction the right, one row per arm (injection $\times 10$; mild withdrawal $\times 0.1$; harsh withdrawal $\times 0.01$), and the pre-toggle traces coincide by construction. (Top row) Injection flips the ring at the toggle---from ${\sim }0.5$ Buy and $0$ Sell in the control to $0$ Buy and ${\sim }1.0$ Sell---and the flipped state decays back over the following $100$--$200$ steps as the EMA bands catch up with the supported price. (Middle and bottom rows) Withdrawal transiently deepens an already-engaged brake: the control ring sits near $0.46$ Buy after onset, either cut lifts the Buy fraction to ${\sim }0.72$--$0.74$ before the transient excess dissipates by ${\sim }200$ steps, and the Sell fraction---which in this loose configuration declines from ${\sim }0.37$ well before onset to zero just after---remains indistinguishable between control and toggled throughout}{figure.caption.62}{}}
